.\" IceBurger Tetris manual page
.\" View without installing: man ./tetris.6
.TH TETRIS 6 "2026-10-31" "IceBurger Tetris" "Games Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
tetris \- IceBurger Tetris, a falling-blocks game made of ice cream and burgers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tetris
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tetris
is a falling-blocks puzzle game built with SDL2.
Every block is a soft-serve cone or a burger, the score is counted in
calories, and cleared lines spray food across the screen.
.PP
Pieces rotate under the Super Rotation System (SRS) with its standard wall
kicks, are dealt from a shuffled bag of all seven shapes, and can be held
once per turn.
A grounded piece may slide for
.B 0.5
seconds before it locks; each successful move or rotation restarts that
timer, up to 15 times per piece.
A ghost outline shows where the current piece will land, and the next five
pieces are shown on the right.
.PP
The window can be resized freely; the picture scales and stays sharp on
high-DPI displays.
The game pauses itself when the window loses focus.
.PP
There are no command-line options.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS Keyboard
.TP 14
.B Left, Right
Move.
Holding a key auto-repeats after 170\~ms, then every 50\~ms.
.TP
.B Down
Soft drop (repeats while held).
.TP
.B Space
Hard drop: fall straight down and lock.
.TP
.B Up, X
Rotate clockwise.
.TP
.B Z
Rotate counter-clockwise.
.TP
.B C, Shift
Hold the current piece, or swap it with the held one.
.TP
.B P, F1
Pause or resume.
.TP
.B R
Start a new game.
.TP
.B M
Mute or unmute sound.
.TP
.B Esc
Quit.
.SS Gamepad
Any controller SDL recognises is picked up when it is connected.
.TP 14
.B D-pad, left stick
Move left or right; down soft-drops.
.TP
.B D-pad up
Hard drop.
.TP
.B A
Rotate clockwise.
.TP
.B B
Rotate counter-clockwise.
.TP
.B X, Y, shoulders
Hold.
.TP
.B Start
Pause or resume.
.TP
.B Back
Start a new game.
.SH SCORING
Each cleared cell is worth 550\~kcal if it is a burger and 250\~kcal if it is
an ice cream.
The total for a clear is then multiplied by the number of lines cleared at
once:
.RS
.nf
.ta 10n
1 line	\(mu1
2 lines	\(mu1.25
3 lines	\(mu1.5
4 lines	\(mu2
.fi
.RE
.PP
A soft drop adds 1\~kcal per row and a hard drop 2\~kcal per row.
The level rises every 10 lines.
Pieces fall one row every 900\~ms at level 0, 70\~ms faster per level, and
never faster than every 90\~ms.
.SH BONUSES
.TP 14
.B Combo Meal
A cleared row made entirely of burgers is worth double.
.TP
.B Brain Freeze
A cleared row made entirely of ice cream halves the falling speed for
5 seconds.
.TP
.B Happy Meal
Clearing four lines at once earns the \(mu2 multiplier, a burp and a
screen shake.
.SH LEVELS
The level names follow the meal:
.B SALAD
(levels 0\(en2),
.B SNACK
(3\(en5),
.B DRIVE-THRU
(6\(en8) and
.B FOOD COMA
(9 and above).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/iceburger/highscores.txt
The five best scores, one per line, highest first.
When
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is unset this is
.IR ~/.local/share/iceburger/highscores.txt .
On macOS it is
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/iceburger/highscores.txt" .
Delete the file to reset the table.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Where the high-score directory is created (Linux and other Unix systems).
.TP
.B SDL_AUDIODRIVER, SDL_VIDEODRIVER
Standard SDL2 variables for choosing the audio and video back ends.
If no audio device can be opened the game runs silently.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a normal quit; 1 if SDL, the window or the renderer cannot be
initialised, or memory runs out at start-up.
